The lowest-indexed critical language is the lowest indexed consistent language, if such a language exists. Thereafter, critical languages are defined inductively in increasing index order. Having determined which languages $L_j$ with $j < i$ are critical, we declare $L_i$ to be \emph{critical} if the following two conditions hold:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item $L_i$ is consistent;
        \item $L_i \subseteq L_j$ for every critical language $L_j$ with $j < i$.
    \end{itemize}
